            <ArticleTitle>Self-terminating ventricular fibrillation during variant angina--a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>581-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors present a case report of self-terminating ventricular fibrillation during an episode of variant angina. The causes of ventricular fibrillation in this disorder and the possible mechanisms for its rare spontaneous interruption are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
